{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrvW6gMcrAbZ7wVkBoEc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `cachelib/lru.py` to the spec and added 14 tests in `tests/test_lru.py`. All 14 pass (`python -m pytest tests -q`).\n\nImplementation choices:\n\n- **Storage:** an `OrderedDict` where the end is most recently used. Get, put, delete and contains are O(1) on average.\n- **TTL:** each entry stores its expiry time at put. An entry counts as expired when `clock() >= expires_at`. An update via `put` resets the expiry.\n- **Expired entries:** `get` counts a miss and an expiration. `contains` and `delete` remove an expired entry and count an expiration, but do not touch hits or misses. `delete` on an expired key returns `False`.\n- **`__len__`:** returns the stored count, which can include expired entries not yet touched. Counting only live entries would need an O(n) scan, which the spec rules out. If you want live-only counts, that's a spec change.\n- **Constructor:** `capacity <= 0` raises `ValueError`.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4610,"cache_read_input_tokens":50957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4610},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02e10880-d4ff-49fc-be99-36ca1ccedafe","uuid":"b2cd121b-a000-4582-a9ba-f57c4f5104d1","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:46:10.822Z","request_id":"req_011CfrvW6NW4jJEJKvJ9kZsA"}
